       tems, the kernel must be configured with the CCOONNFFIIGG__TTMMPPFFSS option.

       The ttmmppffss filesystem supports extended attributes (see  xxaattttrr(7)),  but
       _u_s_e_r extended attributes are not permitted.

       An internal shared memory filesystem is used for System V shared memory
       (sshhmmggeett(2))  and shared anonymous mappings (mmmmaapp(2) with the MMAAPP__SSHHAARREEDD
       and MMAAPP__AANNOONNYYMMOOUUSS flags).  This filesystem is available  regardless  of
       whether the kernel was configured with the CCOONNFFIIGG__TTMMPPFFSS option.

